  "note": "The technologies without a step of the tree yet (D7: apart until lot 2 of the tree; T347, from medieval.json and era3..era9.json). What their files said: medieval.json: The medieval technologies and buildings (docs/PLAN_SIMULACION_NATURAL.md §9), drawn with the Medieval Village MegaKit (assets/models/medieval_kit; visuals written by tools/make_kit_buildings.py). T181: there are no eras; masonry is in era4.json (with writing). era2.json: Faith (V5, docs/VISION_MUNDO_VIVO.md; T181: one file of the game's one pack, no eras): a need of a grown society (a clan that knows rites and has 20 living), with its verb (pray) and the temple where it is done. None of it needs code. D34: tin, bronze and alloying moved to tree_neolithic.json (the lot of the tree that holds the first metals). era3.json: Era 3, the Iron Age (V8): iron ore, which most lands have but deep, forged into tools for everyone. era4.json: Era 4, the classical age (V8): writing on clay tablets, a school where people study, and the need to learn. era5.json: Era 5, the Renaissance (V8): paper and the press; knowledge is copied and travels. Its era follows the Middle Ages (masonry, in era1). era6.json: Era 6, the industrial age (V8): coal, steel and steam; the factory makes what hands made. era7.json: Era 7, the electric age (V8): copper wire and dynamos; a power station lights the town. era8.json: Era 8, the information age (V8): sand made silicon, chips and computers; an office where people work with knowledge. era9.json: Era 9, the arrival of AI (V8): a data centre; machines do work and decide, and people need a purpose (what is left for them is a question each culture answers).",
